  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Soldierpoint Digital Health has received $355M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The company won 88 awards with an average award size of $4M, and obligations are up 53.6% year over year. Fiscal-year history shows no recorded obligations from FY21 through FY24, $231M in FY25, and $355M in FY26. Computer Systems Design Services is the dominant market with $318M in obligations. Electronic Computer Manufacturing is the second market with $36.8M in obligations. The current-year totals are partial and reflect fiscal year to date activity. The mix of large systems-design obligations and electronic-manufacturing work shapes the vendor profile for federal buyers. Contract counts and the average award size point to multiple mid-sized awards rather than a single large contract driving the totals.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Soldierpoint Digital Health's federal business changed year over year?",
        "body": "Soldierpoint Digital Health's obligations are up 53.6% year over year. The company recorded $231M in FY25 and $355M in FY26. The FY26 total represents the current fiscal year to date and follows four fiscal years with no recorded obligations. The rise reflects a shift from zero reported obligations in earlier fiscal years to significant activity in FY25 and FY26."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where is Soldierpoint Digital Health's federal business concentrated?",
        "body": "Computer Systems Design Services is the largest market with $318M in obligations. Electronic Computer Manufacturing is the second market with $36.8M in obligations. Those two NAICS categories account for the majority of the $355M in FY26 obligations. The mix indicates concentration in systems design and electronics manufacturing work."
      }
